{
  "subject": "Basic Mathematics",
  "topic": "Inequalities",
  "introduction": "Inequalities require special care: multiplying/dividing by a negative number flips the inequality sign. Quadratic and rational inequalities are solved by finding critical points and testing sign in each interval (sign chart method). SIMAK often features rational inequalities and simultaneous inequalities.",
  "key_formulas": [
    {
      "name": "Flipping rule",
      "formula": "\\text{If } a > b \\text{ and } c < 0, \\text{ then } ac < bc"
    },
    {
      "name": "Quadratic solution",
      "formula": "ax^2+bx+c > 0: \\text{ find roots, test intervals}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Rational inequality",
      "formula": "\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)} > 0: \\text{ find zeros of both, sign chart}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Absolute value",
      "formula": "|x| < a \\Leftrightarrow -a < x < a"
    },
    {
      "name": "Absolute value (>)",
      "formula": "|x| > a \\Leftrightarrow x > a \\text{ or } x < -a"
    }
  ],
  "tips_and_tricks": [
    "Never multiply both sides by a variable without checking its sign!",
    "For rational inequalities: bring everything to one side, factor numerator and denominator.",
    "Sign chart: mark critical points on number line, test one point per interval.",
    "Quadratic ax²+bx+c > 0 with a>0: outside the roots (x<r₁ or x>r₂).",
    "Quadratic ax²+bx+c < 0 with a>0: between the roots (r₁<x<r₂).",
    "For |x-a| < b: read as -b < x-a < b → a-b < x < a+b."
  ],
  "worked_examples": [
    {
      "title": "Example 1: Rational inequality (SIMAK style)",
      "question": "Solve: (x+2)/(x-1) > 1.",
      "solution": [
        "Step 1: Move 1 to left: (x+2)/(x-1) - 1 > 0.",
        "Step 2: Combine: (x+2-(x-1))/(x-1) > 0 → 3/(x-1) > 0.",
        "Step 3: 3/(x-1) > 0 iff x-1 > 0 → x > 1.",
        "Step 4: Solution: x > 1 (but x ≠ 1, which is already excluded)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Example 2: Quadratic inequality setup",
      "question": "Find all integers x satisfying x²-5x+6 < 0.",
      "solution": [
        "Step 1: Factor: (x-2)(x-3) < 0.",
        "Step 2: Critical points: x=2 and x=3.",
        "Step 3: Sign chart: positive for x<2, negative for 2<x<3, positive for x>3.",
        "Step 4: Solution: 2 < x < 3.",
        "Step 5: Integer solutions: none (no integer strictly between 2 and 3)."
      ]
    }
  ],
